/**

@page applications_exahype2_shallow_water_tohoku_tsunami 2011 Tōhoku Tsunami

The goal of the simulation is to study the generation and open-ocean propagation of the tsunami waves triggered by the Tōhoku
earthquake, with particular focus on their evolution over realistic bathymetry.

The underlying mathematical model is the two-dimensional nonlinear shallow-water equations,
formulated in terms of the water depth \f$ h \f$, the depth-averaged momenta  \f$ hu \f$ and
\f$ hv \f$, and the sea-floor topography \f$ z \f$. The computational domain is a rectangular
ocean region of size \f$ 4 \times 10^6 m \f$ by \f$ 4 \times 10^6 m \f$, discretised on an adaptively refined
Cartesian grid. The bathymetry before the earthquake and the coseismic seafloor displacement are read from NetCDF
data sets.

\image html tohoku-tsunami.gif

*/
